~/.ard/repos/<owner>/<repo>.git`, see Local-executor details) `ard serve` resolves `origin/main` to a SHA and reads `config.yaml` and the role directories from that commit, not from the working tree. It exports them into a snapshot at `~/.ard/config/<owner>/<repo>/<sha>/`, kept 24 hours after a newer SHA replaces it, because roles run from a host path: a role directory, its `Dockerfile` and the scan worktree must all describe the one commit the tick's jobs use. Editing the host's working tree therefore changes nothing on a running controller, with one exception: a local `paused: true` is honoured (see the kill switch), and only that key is read locally. A merged change applies on the next tick without a pull. Symlinks and submodules under the role directories are rejected, and a config that cannot be fetched or does not validate counts as paused. If `origin/main` cannot be loaded at startup, `ard serve` starts paused instead of exiting, posts the load error to the status issue once per distinct error, and retries every tick; no loop runs until a config has loaded. `ard config check` validates the working tree, for authoring; `ard config check --ref <ref>` validates a commit of the local checkout (for example `--ref origin/main` after `git fetch`) without fetching.\n \ndiff --git a/internal/config/load_test.go b/internal/config/load_test.go\nindex 52f9922..0c3caba 100644\n--- a/internal/config/load_test.go\n+++ b/internal/config/load_test.go\n@@ -943,3 +943,23 @@ func TestLLMScannerRules(t *testing.T) {\n \t\t})\n \t}\n }\n+\n+func TestReadsHistory(t *testing.T) {\n+\tfsys := baseFS()\n+\tfsys[\".ard/scanners/cve/history\"] = &fstest.MapFile{Data: nil, Mode: 0o644}\n+\tfsys[\".ard/scanners/lint/history\"] = &fstest.MapFile{Data: nil, Mode: 0o644} // LLM scanner: ignored\n+\tfsys[\".ard/triage/lead/history\"] = &fstest.MapFile{Data: nil, Mode: 0o644}   // not a scanner: ignored\n+\tres := mustLoad(t, fsys)\n+\tgot := map[string]bool{}\n+\tfor _, r := range res.Roles {