{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XmC5GKtTMNFnhvLh3fiX3x","type":"tool_result","content":"6:Design choice (for a maintainer to confirm): a read-only mount of the controller's bare clone (`Job.RepoDir`), not a `git bundle`. The clone is already a full, non-shallow bare repo (`internal/servecmd/clone.go`, `gitx.FetchRef`), so nothing is copied, and git objects are append-only so a concurrent fetch is safe. A bundle can replace the mount later behind the same `Paths.History` field.\n8:1. `internal/executor/executor.go`: add `Job.History bool` (new; job may read git history). Add `History string` to `Paths` (new; where the job sees the bare clone) and `HistoryDir string` to `Handle` (new; host path, \"\" = none). Old stored handles decode with the zero value.\n10:3. `internal/executor/local/local.go` `Prepare`: when `j.History`, set `h.HistoryDir = j.RepoDir` and `h.View.History = j.RepoDir` (host mode). In the Dockerfile branch set `h.View.History = \"/history\"`, keeping Work/Role/ConfigDir as today.\n11:4. `internal/executor/local/docker.go` `runArgv`: when `h.HistoryDir != \"\"` append `-v <HistoryDir>:/history:ro`. `internal/executor/local/env.go` `ardEnv`: add `ARD_HISTORY=<View.History>` when set. Never mount it writable. Add `-e GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=1 -e GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0=safe.directory -e GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0=/history` (fixed values, not secrets) so git accepts the mount; confirm in the Docker integration test whether it is needed.\n15:   - `Dockerfile`: same pins as `scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile` (same base digest, trufflehog 3.100.0, jq 1.8.2, checksums, TMPDIR=/var/tmp). Reuse its comments, including the AGPL note.\n24:11. Kubernetes executor is not in the repo yet: leave a comment on `Paths.History` that a k8s executor must supply a read-only copy (for example an init container running `git clone --mirror` or a bundle volume).\n29:- `internal/executor/local/local_test.go`: host-mode `Prepare` with `History` gives `View.History == RepoDir`; without it both are empty.\n30:- `internal/executor/local/docker_test`-style argv test (see `runArgv` tests in `misc_test.go`/`local_test.go`): argv contains `-v <repo>:/history:ro` only when `HistoryDir` is set, never without `:ro`; `ARD_HISTORY=/history` in env.\n31:- `internal/executor/local/docker_integration_test.go` (skipped without Docker): a container with History runs `git --git-dir /history log --all` and sees more than one commit; a write to `/history` fails.\n34:- `internal/roles/roles_test.go`: add the new files to the embedded file list (line 32), `scan` executable (line 46), and a `TestEmbeddedTrufflehogHistoryRoleLoadsAsScanner` checking Every 168h, Autoclose false, MaxOpen 5, Route needs-human, a Dockerfile and the timeout.\n35:- New `internal/roles/trufflehog_history_test.go`, reusing the fake-binary helpers in `trufflehog_test.go`: (a) same secret in HEAD-scanner and history-scanner output yields the same fingerprint; (b) a git-source result is projected with file/line only; (c) no marker string (Raw, RawV2, Redacted, SecretParts, ExtraData, commit, email) appears in stdout, stderr or any temp file; (d) fails closed: trufflehog exit non-zero, missing \"finished scanning\" summary, count mismatch, a result without Git metadata, bad allow entry; (e) argv contains no `--since-commit`, `--max-depth`, `--filter-*`, `--results`, and contains `--no-verification`; (f) missing `ARD_HISTORY` is a failure; missing tool exits 2; (g) Dockerfile pins.\n39:Medium. Executor change touches the job sandbox: the mount must stay `:ro` and scanner-only, and history includes every fetched ref, such as unmerged PR branches. The scanner handles raw secrets in pipes, so the no-leak tests are essential. No protected path in `merge.protected_paths` is touched (the new role lives under `internal/roles/`, not `.ard/scanners/`; the `Dockerfile` rule matches only the root-level file). A repository that wants the scanner running still needs a maintainer-made `.ard/scanners/trufflehog-history/` copy and `.ard/config.yaml` override. No migration; old handles keep working. Concurrency: the scan reads the clone while fetches run, which git tolerates.\n42:L. Files: `internal/executor/executor.go`, `internal/executor/validate.go`, `internal/executor/local/{local,docker,env}.go`, `internal/config/types.go`, `internal/scanner/engine_exec.go`, `internal/roles/{roles.go,config.yaml}`, `internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog-history/{Dockerfile,history,scan,findings.jq,exclude-paths}`, `internal/initcmd/body.go`, docs, and the matching tests. Roughly 900 to 1,300 changed lines, mostly the copied scan script, jq and tests; it can be split into the executor part and the scanner part if it passes the warn limit.\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*_test.go\n48:\t// admin in. A handle whose RepoDir differs (stored before #113, when\n49:\t// RepoDir was the operator's checkout) has its worktree made writable and\n51:\t// executor.cleanup_foreign_repo Info log. \"\" = always use h.RepoDir.\n169:\tsha, err := l.git.RevParse(ctx, j.RepoDir, j.Ref)\n185:\t\tWorktree: wt, Home: home, RepoDir: j.RepoDir, BaseSHA: sha,\n199:\t\t\tif rerr := l.git.WorktreeRemove(context.WithoutCancel(ctx), j.RepoDir, wt, true); rerr != nil {\n203:\t\t\tl.git.WorktreePrune(context.WithoutCancel(ctx), j.RepoDir)\n214:\tif err = l.git.WorktreeAdd(ctx, j.RepoDir, wt, sha); err != nil {\n258:\t\th.HistoryDir, h.View.History = j.RepoDir, j.RepoDir","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b70ba2b-fa8e-4d9b-b737-89695e409a9f","uuid":"8888c534-6c89-448b-8329-74594e11dec0","timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:11:53.129Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"6:Design choice (for a maintainer to confirm): a read-only mount of the controller's bare clone (`Job.RepoDir`), not a `git bundle`. The clone is already a full, non-shallow bare repo (`internal/servecmd/clone.go`, `gitx.FetchRef`), so nothing is copied, and git objects are append-only so a concurrent fetch is safe